Let lldb run on Windows XP (32-bit, MinGW with libstdc++).

- lldb/Host/windows/windows.h includes XPCompat.h (patch 0001).
- MainLoopWindows: the thread HANDLE of a libstdc++ std::thread comes from
  pthread_gethandle; without CancelIoEx (XP) the pipe monitor polls instead
  of blocking in a read that could not be cancelled.
- HostThreadWindows calls the GetThreadId stand-in by name (lldb has
  methods of that name, so there is no macro).
- ProcessRunLock uses std::shared_mutex instead of an SRWLOCK.
- SocketAddress's own inet_ntop gets its own name, so that the calls do not
  bind to the ws2_32.dll import.
- ProcessWindows names the main module through QueryFullProcessImageNameW
  when GetModuleFileNameExW cannot yet (XP, at the create-process event);
  without it the main thread was never registered and nothing stopped.

diff -Nru a/lldb/include/lldb/Host/windows/windows.h b/lldb/include/lldb/Host/windows/windows.h
--- a/lldb/include/lldb/Host/windows/windows.h	2026-11-17 13:31:38.742262100 -0600
+++ b/lldb/include/lldb/Host/windows/windows.h	2026-11-17 13:31:38.634919300 -0600
@@ -29,4 +29,9 @@
 #define FAR
 #define NEAR
 
+// Run-time fallbacks for the Vista and later APIs used here (Windows XP).
+// HostThreadWindows has a GetThreadId method and calls the fallback by name.
+#define LLVM_XPCOMPAT_NO_GETTHREADID_MACRO
+#include "llvm/Support/Windows/XPCompat.h"
+
 #endif // LLDB_lldb_windows_h_
diff -Nru a/lldb/source/Host/common/SocketAddress.cpp b/lldb/source/Host/common/SocketAddress.cpp
--- a/lldb/source/Host/common/SocketAddress.cpp	2026-11-17 13:31:39.601225300 -0600
+++ b/lldb/source/Host/common/SocketAddress.cpp	2026-11-17 13:31:39.493055500 -0600
@@ -32,6 +32,11 @@
 // WindowsXP needs an inet_ntop implementation
 #ifdef _WIN32
 
+// Under its own name: the Windows headers declare inet_ntop as an import
+// from ws2_32.dll (Vista and later) once _WIN32_WINNT is high enough, and
+// the calls below would bind to that.
+#define inet_ntop lldb_inet_ntop
+
 #ifndef INET6_ADDRSTRLEN // might not be defined in older Windows SDKs
 #define INET6_ADDRSTRLEN 46
 #endif
